CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
In an atomic section, A[k]++ with k read from shared memory reads and writes
back every element of A, the reads and writes of A[i] each under k == i. The
write was recorded as made under the path guard alone, so the later read of
A[0] in the same section reused the written-back value, which for k != 0 is
the value of a read that did not happen: unconstrained. A[0] could be read
as anything. The write is now recorded under its event condition, and a later
read not covered by an earlier access takes a fresh generation with its event
on that generation.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after, with --por and --no-por.
Reduced from pthread-complex/elimination_backoff_stack (no-overflow).

See atomic_symbolic_index_reread_other_write and
atomic_symbolic_index_reread_own_write, real failures that must stay FAILED.
